-time high is 119\u00b0F, on July 6, 2024.","t_chg":"Redding's nights cooled over the long run but have warmed since 1986. Its days have warmed.","p_chg":"Across 116 complete years: Redding's average low has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.08\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.16 to \u22120.00), about \u22121.1\u00b0F since 1894. Redding's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.30\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.23 to +0.37), about +3.9\u00b0F since 1894. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.80\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.53 to +1.08) and highs have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.69\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.26 to +1.12). The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in none; 3 months fell. Highs rose in 9 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Redding has gotten drier","p_rain":"Redding's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.84 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22121.54 to \u22120.15), about \u221210.9 inches since 1896. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 33.5 inches a year. The wettest year was 1983 (78.05 in); the driest, 2013 (12.80 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":false},"t_year":"2026 so far: 5 daily record highs, no daily record lows"}}